# AI Clinical Assistant Center

This is the generated application README for the full Tkinter GUI in `client_medgemma_patients_mcp.py`. It matches the project documentation in `../md/README.md`.

The application provides a two-column **AI Clinical Assistant Center**: patient/date-time selection above assistant controls and response on the left, with framed selectable X-ray tiles, readable EKG images, and selectable blood-test result tables on the right. It retrieves records through the separate local MCP client and submits only selected original records to MedGemma through the configured Ollama endpoint.

## Run

From the project root:

```bat
py -m pip install -r python\requirements.txt
py python\client_medgemma_patients_mcp.py
```

Keep `.env` and `patient_records` beside this directory. Configure `OLLAMA_URL`, `MEDGEMMA_MODEL`, `PATIENT_RECORDS_DIR`, and optional display dimensions there. The local MCP server IDs default to `XRAY_SERVER_ID=xrays`, `EKG_SERVER_ID=ekgs`, and `BLOODTEST_SERVER_ID=blood_tests`. Patient folders support `xrays`, `ekgs`, and `blood_tests`, including dated snapshots and legacy `data/<modality>` folders.

Search in the app with the patient's first name, last name, and eight-digit DOB (`MMDDYYYY`). Search validates the full date and maps the four-digit year to the existing two-digit patient-folder suffix. A successful search loads the newest snapshot; a missing patient displays an error. The far-right active-patient block shows `Active patient` in teal, with the selected name and DOB below in coral. Use the in-app **Choose date & time** picker to load another snapshot for that patient. The **Ask AI** button submits the selected evidence and question. Only explicit selections are sent; X-rays are sent before EKGs. Generated reports require clinician review.
